0,Latji-Latji language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ladji_Ladji_language,"October 16, 2025 - Ladji Ladji (Ledji-Ledji) is a moribund Australian Aboriginal language once widely spoken in New South Wales and Victoria by the Latjilatji (or Ladji Ladji) people.",Ladji Ladji,Australian
1,Latji Latji - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Latji_Latji,"March 26, 2026 - The Ladji Ladji lived on the Murray River in the Mildura area. White settlement of that area occurred in 1845–7. The early explorer Edward Eyre mentioned them in his work (1845) under the name Boraipar and transcribed a number of words from their language.",Ladji Ladji,Australian
2,Latji-Latji dialect - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ledji-Ledji_language,"March 7, 2026 - Ladji Ladji (Ledji-Ledji) is a moribund Australian Aboriginal language once widely spoken in New South Wales and Victoria by the Latjilatji (or Ladji Ladji) people.",Ladji Ladji,Australian
3,Ladidi Ladida - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ladidi_Ladida,"December 26, 2025 - ""Ladidi Ladida"" is a song by Danish pop music duo S.O.A.P., released as the second single from their debut album Not Like Other Girls (1998). The single reached No. 8 in New Zealand and No. 15 in Australia, where it is certified gold. The song was written by Remee Zhivago.",Ladji Ladji,Australian
